   "name": "boswellia.md",
   "text": "title: Boswellia\naka: Boswellia serrata, Indian frankincense\ntags: plant medicinal herb\nwarn: Consult a healthcare provider before use, especially if pregnant, breastfeeding, managing asthma, or taking medications, as interactions remain unclear.\nsource: https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/boswellia, as summarised by Project NOMAD (natural_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/natural_remedies.json#boswellia\n\nBoswellia resin extract is traditionally used to reduce inflammation and pain, and is promoted as a dietary supplement to support joint health and mobility, particularly for osteoarthritis.\n\n## how\nBoswellia is taken orally as a dietary supplement. Clinical trials have used doses up to 1,000 mg daily for up to 6 months; follow the product label and consult a healthcare provider before starting.\n\n## evidence\nSome studies suggest oral boswellia may help reduce inflammation and pain associated with osteoarthritis, but larger rigorous trials are needed; topical use lacks sufficient evidence of effectiveness.\n\n## safety\nExtracts up to 1,000 mg daily have been used safely in clinical trials lasting up to 6 months. Consult a healthcare provider before use, especially if pregnant, breastfeeding, managing asthma, or taking medications, as interactions remain unclear.\n\n## used for\n- Muscle & joint pain\n\n## also said\n- indian frankincense for my knees\n- tree resin supplement for arthritis, any proof\n- osteoarthritis stiff joints, is the incense tree extract worth trying\n- how many mg of boswellia per day\n- how long can i take the resin capsules for joints\n- i have asthma and want a joint supplement, is the resin one ok\n- boswelia for inflammation\n- resin pills for joint mobility in old age\n- does a resin cream work on sore joints\n- 1000 mg resin extract daily is that too much\n- breastfeeding, can i take the incense resin extract\n- tree gum for arthritis pain, does it reduce inflammation\n- my dad's hips are stiff, someone said take frankincense\n- is it safe to take boswellia for 6 months\n- resin extract for joints, will it interact with my pills\n- rubbing the resin gel on the knee, useful or not\n- incense resin as a natural anti inflammatory for joints\n- pregnant, can i take frankincense for my joints\n- gum resin capsule for arthritic hands\n- the resin they burn in church, can you take it for joint pain\n- salai guggal for joint pain\n"
