   "name": "clean-and-cover-wounds.md",
   "text": "title: Clean and cover wounds and cuts\ntags: health remedy\nwarn: Seek immediate care for wounds that are deep, gaping, caused by an animal or human bite, or associated with a puncture from a potentially contaminated object (tetanus risk).\nsource: https://medlineplus.gov/firstaid.html, as summarised by Project NOMAD (home_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/home_remedies.json#clean-and-cover-wounds\n\nFor minor cuts and scrapes, rinse the wound thoroughly with cool clean water to remove dirt, apply gentle pressure with gauze to stop bleeding, then cover with a clean bandage. Wash with soap and water to reduce infection risk.\n\n## how\nApply firm but gentle pressure with gauze to stop bleeding; if blood soaks through, add more gauze on top without removing the first layer. Rinse the wound with cool clean water, then cover it with a clean dry bandage.\n\n## evidence\nCDC guidance on wound care states: put pressure on a bleeding cut until it stops, gently pour clean water over the wound to clean it, then apply a clean, dry bandage. MedlinePlus (NLM) similarly advises rinsing cuts with cool water and applying firm but gentle pressure to stop bleeding.\n\n## safety\nWatch for signs of infection in the days following — increasing redness, swelling, warmth, pus, or red streaks spreading from the wound require prompt medical evaluation. Seek immediate care for wounds that are deep, gaping, caused by an animal or human bite, or associated with a puncture from a potentially contaminated object (tetanus risk).\n\n## used for\n- Wounds & cuts\n\n## also said\n- cut my finger with a knife\n- deep cut wont stop bleeding\n- how to stop bleeding from a cut\n- kid fell and scraped his knee\n- scraped my arm on rocks, dirty\n- how to clean a wound with no antiseptic\n- should i wash a cut with soap\n- blood soaking through the bandage\n- how to bandage a cut\n- cut is red and swollen a few days later\n- pus coming out of the cut\n- red lines spreading from a wound\n- stepped on a rusty nail\n- dog bit me\n- cut is gaping open, need stitches?\n- wound infected signs\n- grazed hand falling off bike\n- sliced my hand with an axe\n- elderly mother cut her leg and skin is thin\n- gash on leg far from hospital\n- i cut me with glass, blood a lot\n- cleaned the cut, now what\n"
