   "name": "dandelion.md",
   "text": "title: Dandelion\naka: dandelions, taraxacum, pissenlit, lowenzahn\ntags: plant wild food\nwarn: Avoid lawns, parks and roadsides that may be sprayed or polluted.\nsee: foraging-rules\nsource: compiled from general foraging references, verify before relying on it\n\nAlmost every part of the dandelion is edible. It grows nearly everywhere and is available most of the year.\n\n## identify\nA flat rosette of leaves with deep, backward-pointing teeth, growing from a single root. Each yellow flower sits alone on a hollow, leafless stem. Broken stems and leaves release white milky sap. The seed head is a round white \"clock\".\n\nSimilar plants such as cat's-ear and hawkbit have hairier leaves or branched stems. They are not dangerous.\n\n## eat\nYoung leaves are best raw in salad. Older leaves are bitter: boil them and discard the water. Flowers are edible raw, in batter or as tea. Roots can be cooked like a vegetable.\n\n## harvest\nLeaves are mildest in early spring and late autumn. Pick flowers in full sun when open. Dig roots in autumn.\n\n## use\nRoasted, ground roots make a coffee substitute.\n\n## also said\n- dandelion\n- dandelion leaves\n- pissenlit\n- yellow flower with milky sap, can I eat it\n- the yellow flower on lawns everywhere, is it food\n- leaves with jagged teeth pointing backwards growing flat on the ground\n- white fluffy seed ball plant edible?\n- dandelion salad bitter\n- my dandelion greens taste so bitter how to fix\n- can you eat the root of dandelion\n- how to make coffee from roots\n- coffee substitute from wild plants\n- roasted root coffee\n- can i eat dandelion flowers raw\n- dandelion flower tea\n- fried flowers in batter which plant\n- when are dandelion leaves least bitter\n- best time to dig dandelion roots\n- kids picked dandelions in the park can we eat them\n- is it safe to eat dandelions from the lawn by the road\n- the one with hollow stem and white milk inside\n- plant like dandelion but hairy leaves is it poisonous\n- cats ear or dandelion how tell apart\n- hawkbit looks like dandelion is it bad\n- what parts of a dandelion are edible\n- wild green that grows everywhere almost all year\n- old dandelion leaves too tough\n- pick flowers when sunny?\n- the flowers close up when its cloudy, still good to pick?\n- weed with yellow flowers and white sap all over the garden\n- we have tons of these yellow flowers in the field can we use them\n- can i cook dandelion root like carrot\n- blowball plant leaves salad\n- the flower stem has no leaves and is hollow, which plant is that\n- taraxacum edible parts\n- boil the old leaves and throw water?\n- my child ate a dandelion flower is that ok\n"
