   "name": "dark-quiet-room-headache.md",
   "text": "title: Rest in a dark, quiet room (for headache)\ntags: health remedy\nwarn: Sudden severe ('thunderclap') headache, headache with fever, stiff neck, confusion, or vision changes may signal a serious condition and require emergency evaluation.\nsource: https://medlineplus.gov/headache.html, as summarised by Project NOMAD (home_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/home_remedies.json#dark-quiet-room-headache\n\nResting with eyes closed in a dark, quiet room is a recommended non-medication self-care measure during a headache or migraine. Drinking water to prevent dehydration and placing a cool cloth on the forehead are often combined with this rest.\n\n## how\nGo to a quiet, darkened room, close your eyes, and rest. Drink water and place a cool damp cloth on your forehead to help ease discomfort.\n\n## evidence\nMedlinePlus (NLM) describes resting in a quiet, darkened room as one of the key things you can do to feel better during a headache or migraine, alongside drinking water and using relaxation techniques. These recommendations are attributed to NIH sources on headache and migraine management.\n\n## safety\nSudden severe ('thunderclap') headache, headache with fever, stiff neck, confusion, or vision changes may signal a serious condition and require emergency evaluation. Frequent headaches that disrupt daily life should be discussed with a healthcare provider rather than managed solely at home.\n\n## used for\n- Headache\n- Sleeplessness\n\n## also said\n- bad headache and no painkillers\n- migraine coming on\n- head pounding, light hurts my eyes\n- migraine with noise sensitivity\n- how to get rid of a headache without pills\n- headache from the sun and heat\n- kid has a headache\n- tension headache what helps\n- sudden worst headache of my life\n- headache with stiff neck and fever\n- headache and blurry vision\n- head hurts so much i feel sick\n- headache every day\n- what to do during a migraine\n- lie down in the dark for headache\n- headache and confused\n- grandma has a strong headache\n- throbbing head, need relief\n- headache from dehydration\n- cool cloth on forehead for headache\n- my head hurt very much, help\n- migrane attack no medicine\n"
