   "name": "humidifier-and-steam.md",
   "text": "title: Humidifier or steam inhalation\naka: cool-mist vaporizer, steam inhalation\ntags: health remedy\nwarn: Use cool-mist humidifiers rather than warm-mist (steam) versions for children to avoid burn risk. When inhaling steam from hot water, use caution to avoid scalding; keep a safe distance and do not cover your head over a pot of boiling water.\nsource: https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html, as summarised by Project NOMAD (home_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/home_remedies.json#humidifier-and-steam\n\nUsing a clean humidifier or cool-mist vaporizer adds moisture to the air and can help relieve nasal congestion and cough. Breathing steam from a bowl of hot water or a running shower 2–4 times daily also loosens nasal secretions.\n\n## how\nFill a clean cool-mist humidifier or vaporizer with water and run it in the room. Clean the device daily per the manufacturer's instructions to prevent mold and bacteria buildup.\n\n## evidence\nCDC recommends using a clean humidifier or cool-mist vaporizer as a home care measure for common cold symptoms including congestion and cough. MedlinePlus similarly notes that a humidifier can break up mucus and that steam inhalation from a shower is a recognized congestion-relief strategy.\n\n## safety\nClean the humidifier daily per manufacturer instructions to prevent mold and bacterial growth. Use cool-mist humidifiers rather than warm-mist (steam) versions for children to avoid burn risk. When inhaling steam from hot water, use caution to avoid scalding; keep a safe distance and do not cover your head over a pot of boiling water.\n\n## used for\n- Nasal congestion\n- Cough\n- Common cold\n\n## also said\n- stuffy nose and cant breathe at night\n- blocked nose from a cold\n- air is so dry and i keep coughing\n- congested chest, mucus wont come up\n- how to breathe steam for a cold\n- steam from the shower helps congestion?\n- humidifier for a baby with a cold\n- is warm mist ok for kids\n- bowl of hot water over head for blocked nose\n- how to clean a humidifier\n- kid stuffed up and cant sleep\n- nose blocked, no nasal spray\n- thick mucus how to loosen it\n- dry air in the room making me cough\n- stuffy head cold, natural relief\n- vaporizer how to use\n- cant breathe through my nose, very annoying\n- baby congested nose what can i do\n- elderly mom congested and wheezy from a cold\n- steam inhalation safe?\n- mucus stuck in nose and throat\n- nose bloked since days, breath steam good?\n"
