   "name": "lavender.md",
   "text": "title: Lavender\naka: Lavandula angustifolia\ntags: plant medicinal herb\nwarn: Topical application can trigger allergic skin reactions. Potential interactions with sedative drugs warrant discussion with a healthcare provider. Safety during pregnancy and breastfeeding is unknown.\nsource: https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/lavender, as summarised by Project NOMAD (natural_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/natural_remedies.json#lavender\n\nLavender is promoted as an oral supplement and aromatherapy agent for calming anxiety, stress, and sleep difficulties; it is also used topically and in aromatherapy for depression symptoms and pain.\n\n## how\nLavender is used as an oral supplement (capsule or tea), as an aromatherapy oil (inhaled or diffused), or applied topically to skin. Oral lavender oil products have been studied for anxiety; aromatherapy involves inhaling the scent from a diffuser or a few drops on a cloth.\n\n## evidence\nStudies suggest oral lavender oil might be beneficial for anxiety, including anxiety with co-occurring depression; evidence for sleep improvement is insufficient, and it is unclear whether aromatherapy with lavender benefits anxiety, stress, or depression.\n\n## safety\nOral lavender products may cause diarrhea, headache, nausea, or burping. Topical application can trigger allergic skin reactions. Potential interactions with sedative drugs warrant discussion with a healthcare provider. Safety during pregnancy and breastfeeding is unknown.\n\n## used for\n- Sleeplessness\n\n## also said\n- oil in a diffuser for stress\n- few drops on my pillow to calm down\n- scented flower oil capsule for anxiety\n- anxiety with depression, oral oil capsule\n- aromatherapy oil for feeling low\n- does smelling the provence flower help anxiety\n- lavender oil rash on skin\n- lavender with sleeping pills safe\n- lavender while pregnant\n- lavendar for stress\n- calming oil pills made me burp and nauseous\n- scented oil to inhale for pain\n- calming smell for anxious nights\n- fragrant herb tea for nerves\n- rubbing calming flower oil on wrists, any skin risk\n- lavender and benzodiazepines\n- does a fragrant oil diffuser help me sleep\n- breastfeeding and scented flower oil\n- calming oil supplement gave me diarrhea and headache\n- silexan for anxiety\n- drop of essential oil on a cloth to sniff for stress\n"
