   "name": "pinworm-hygiene.md",
   "text": "title: Hygiene measures for pinworm\ntags: health remedy\nsource: https://medlineplus.gov/pinworms.html, as summarised by Project NOMAD (home_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/home_remedies.json#pinworm-hygiene\n\nThorough handwashing with soap and warm water (especially after toilet use and before eating), daily morning bathing with soap and water, daily underwear changes, short and clean fingernails, and laundering of bedding and pajamas in hot water are the key household self-care measures for managing pinworm infection.\n\n## how\nBathe after waking up each morning and wash hands regularly, especially after using the bathroom. Change underwear daily, wash pajamas and bed sheets often, and avoid nail biting to prevent reinfection.\n\n## evidence\nCDC identifies handwashing as 'the most important way to prevent the spread of pinworms.' MedlinePlus (NIH/NIAID) lists bathe after waking up, wash pajamas and bed sheets often, wash hands regularly, change underwear every day, and avoid nail biting and scratching the anal area as the core preventive hygiene steps.\n\n## safety\nHygiene alone typically cannot eliminate an active pinworm infection — over-the-counter antiparasitic medication (pyrantel pamoate) is generally needed, and all household members should be treated simultaneously. Medication is typically repeated after 2 weeks because it kills worms but not eggs; the second dose treats worms that hatched after the first dose.\n\n## used for\n- Pinworm\n\n## also said\n- kid scratching his bottom at night\n- itchy bum at night child\n- tiny white worms in my kids poop\n- saw little worms around her anus\n- pinworms what to do\n- threadworms in children\n- how to get rid of pinworms\n- how do pinworms spread\n- does the whole family need treatment for worms\n- wash sheets for pinworms\n- how to stop pinworms coming back\n- kid bites nails and has worms\n- anal itching worse at night kids\n- worms in kids, no pharmacy\n- pinworm eggs on bedding\n- pinworm medicine second dose why\n- hygiene for worms\n- daughter cant sleep because her bottom itches\n- white threads in stool\n- school kids worms spreading at home\n- my child have worm, what to do\n- do i need medicine for pinworms or is washing enough\n"
