   "name": "sleep-hygiene.md",
   "text": "title: Sleep hygiene practices\naka: good sleep habits\ntags: health remedy\nsource: https://www.cdc.gov/sleep/about/index.html, as summarised by Project NOMAD (home_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/home_remedies.json#sleep-hygiene\n\nA consistent set of behavioral practices — consistent bedtime and wake time, a cool and dark bedroom, avoiding screens and caffeine near bedtime, and regular exercise — helps adults achieve and maintain adequate sleep.\n\n## how\nGo to bed and wake up at the same time every day. Keep the bedroom quiet, dark, and cool; turn off electronic devices at least 30 minutes before bedtime; and avoid caffeine in the afternoon and evening and large meals or alcohol before bed.\n\n## evidence\nCDC and NHLBI both recommend these specific practices for healthy sleep: going to bed and waking at the same time daily, keeping the bedroom quiet, cool, and dark, turning off screens at least 30 minutes before bed, avoiding caffeine in the afternoon and evening, and avoiding large meals or alcohol before sleep. NHLBI notes these habits are particularly important for shift workers and people with insomnia.\n\n## safety\nGood sleep hygiene can help relieve short-term insomnia; persistent insomnia lasting more than a few weeks should be evaluated by a healthcare provider. Sleep difficulties accompanied by snoring, gasping during sleep, or excessive daytime sleepiness may indicate obstructive sleep apnea, which requires medical diagnosis.\n\n## used for\n- Sleeplessness\n\n## also said\n- cant sleep at night\n- lying awake for hours\n- insomnia for weeks\n- how to fall asleep faster\n- wake up at 3am and cant get back to sleep\n- good sleep habits\n- screens before bed bad for sleep?\n- coffee keeps me awake\n- how to fix my sleep schedule\n- shift work messing up my sleep\n- too stressed to sleep\n- room too hot to sleep\n- always tired during the day\n- snoring and gasping in sleep\n- kid wont sleep at night\n- elderly dad sleeps badly\n- does alcohol help sleep\n- same bedtime every day, does it matter\n- how to sleep better without pills\n- sleep problems for a month\n- i dont sleep good, what to do\n- jet lag cant sleep\n"
